# YouTube Data API v3 key, used ONLY by the harvester (scripts/harvest.mjs).
#
# Create one at https://console.cloud.google.com:
#   1. New project
#   2. APIs & Services -> Library -> enable "YouTube Data API v3"
#   3. Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key
#   4. Restrict the key to the YouTube Data API v3
#
# The API is free: 10,000 quota units/day, a hard cap rather than a meter. There is no
# per-request charge and no billing to enable.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill it in. The site itself never uses
# this key — it only ever reads the pre-built pool.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# Optional: address for content reports. It is INLINED INTO THE PUBLIC BUNDLE — a mailto
# link cannot work otherwise — so use a disposable alias you can retire if it gets
# scraped. Leave blank to disable the report half; the control still hides videos locally.
# A malformed value is treated as blank (but is still published), so set it carefully.
VITE_REPORT_EMAIL=
